 visualizes “Intent Bubbles”—zones of the motor cortex lighting up before a physical action is taken.","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"key":"wh6O9A1eOb"}],"key":"HqNoKZKvR6"}],"key":"ubYRHRMhe2"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Synergy: If SciStream detects a lag in the neural-to-digital link, syGlass can highlight the “bottleneck” area in red within the Commander’s field of view, allowing for an immediate tactical swap or mission abort.","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"key":"G8nZ9ijUSn"}],"key":"nK8yG8dzrr"}],"key":"vJmmYp39hO"}],"key":"qWiEAgVv7C"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"“Augmented Intent”","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"key":"ebiIXnJEaC"}],"identifier":"augmented-intent","label":"“Augmented Intent”","html_id":"augmented-intent","implicit":true,"key":"Qj0JFCLBiO"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sensory Injection: The Commander can “push” tactical data directly into the user’s sensory perception. For example, injecting a “thermal sense” or “spatial ping” into the user’s parietal lobe, allowing them to “feel” an enemy’s location without looking at a screen.","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"gaYrnY7gFZ"}],"key":"MtabwZQPPf"}],"key":"pHxMqacjza"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focus Steering: By manipulating the XR dashboard, the Commander can boost the user’s visual processing or auditory gain during high-stress moments, effectively “tuning” the user’s brain for the mission.","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"j0b0LJOqYl"}],"key":"ZrCklsaMsS"}],"key":"YDLFcRUIdK"}],"key":"zAXe7U1Vwx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"For the Physician:","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"key":"bN1tr34N3s"}],"identifier":"for-the-physician","label":"For the Physician:","html_id":"for-the-physician","implicit":true,"key":"xhXnCZrUA9"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"“Precision Diagnostic Suite”","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"key":"nU0b444aI8"}],"identifier":"precision-diagnostic-suite","label":"“Precision Diagnostic Suite”","html_id":"precision-diagnostic-suite","implicit":true,"key":"qFZIBvBvIZ"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":61,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":61,"column":1},"end":{"line":61,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"syGlass Implementation: Enables “Virtual Micro-Slicing.” The Physician can freeze a SciStream live-feed and use syGlass tools to measure the density of neural firing or track electrode degradation in 1:1 scale.","position":{"start":{"line":61,"column":1},"end":{"line":61,"column":1}},"key":"CHDRVPhCLg"}],"key":"eY6MDgT9ky"}],"key":"sWshm3VR1u"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":62,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Synergy: While inside the syGlass VR environment, the Physician can trigger SciX queries via voice command (e.g., “SciX: Show similar activation patterns in recent epilepsy studies”), with the results appearing as floating windows next to the live 3D brain model.","position":{"start":{"line":62,"column":1},"end":{"line":62,"column":1}},"key":"kksDc3mq04"}],"key":"kdsVgP83DW"}],"key":"sIV8Esy3o6"}],"key":"gCCXaMb6Ir"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"position":{"start":{"line":64,"column":1},"end":{"line":64,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"“Sensory Re-Calibration”","position":{"start":{"line":64,"column":1},"end":{"line":64,"column":1}},"key":"FJU4utaXvP"}],"identifier":"sensory-re-calibration","label":"“Sensory Re-Calibration”","html_id":"sensory-re-calibration","implicit":true,"key":"K6eidmufkW"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":65,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tactile Mapping: If a user has lost sensation in a limb, the Physician can use syGlass in XR to manually stimulate specific “dead” zones. By “tapping” a virtual neuron in the XR environment, they send a signal to the NESD to trigger a phantom touch for the user.","position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":65,"column":1}},"key":"qI7MRj4ejH"}],"key":"XdY3NzccV4"}],"key":"H1gGou6UcR"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pain Suppression: The Physician can identify “pain circuits” (hyper-active clusters) and use an XR interface to “dim” those regions, sending inhibitory signals to provide immediate relief.","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"P3ylSB0